# `model::BlackScholes`

Constant-volatility model: one parameter, the volatility.

The geometric Brownian motion `dS = (r − q) S dt + σ S dW` with a single constant volatility `σ`. It prices in closed form (the Analytic engine) and is the reference every other model reduces to (a Heston model with `σ → 0` and `v₀ = θ` collapses to it). Its one parameter is a `Series` of one element.

## Fields

### `volatility`

`pluss::Series`, default `undefined`.

The annual volatility `σ`; must be positive. The price of every option is increasing in it.

## Guidance

Held by `Model` when its kind is `BlackScholes`; accepted by `Field::price`.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

The price of an at-the-money call rises with the volatility.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(5));
  mod::Field field{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(fin::pricing::Call, 100.0, 1.0),
                   .market = fin::market::make(100.0, 0.02, 0.0),
                   .model = fin::model::make(fin::model::Kind::BlackScholes, {0.2}),
                   .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::Analytic, .risk = mod::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  for (const double v : {0.1, 0.2, 0.3, 0.4}) {
    fin::model::BlackScholes m = field.model.as<fin::model::BlackScholes>();
    m.volatility = pluss::make_series({v});
    out.writeln("volatility", v, ": price =", field.price(m).price.items<double>()[0]);
  }
}
```

### Example 2

A model built directly from the struct, then priced.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace fin = pluss::subsp::math::finance;
namespace mod = fin::module;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(5));
  mod::Field field{.instrument = fin::instrument::make(fin::pricing::Call, 100.0, 1.0), .market = fin::market::make(100.0, 0.02, 0.0),
                   .model = fin::model::BlackScholes{.volatility = pluss::make_series({0.25})}, .controls = {.engine = mod::Engine::Analytic, .risk = mod::Risk::PriceOnly}};
  out.writeln(field.model_name(), field.price().price.items<double>());
}
```

